{"name":"Exclusively","hex":"#6b515f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"exclusively","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To the exclusion of anything or anyone else; solely or entirely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclusively"}],"entries":[{"title":"Exclusive (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Exclusive is the second studio album by American singer Chris Brown. It was released on November 6, 2007, by CBE and Jive Records. The record serves as Chris Brown's second studio release under his CBE record label, as well as with Jive. The record also serves as the follow-up to his multi-platinum selling debut album, Chris Brown (2005)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/Chrisexclusive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exclusive_(album)"},{"title":"Exclusive (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Exclusive is a 1937 American crime drama directed by Alexander Hall and written by Jack Moffitt, Sidney Salkow and Rian James. The film stars Fred MacMurray, Frances Farmer, Charlie Ruggles, Lloyd Nolan, Fay Holden and Ralph Morgan. The film was released on August 6, 1937, by Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/52/Exclusive_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exclusive_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bc/Exclusive_-_The_Forever_Edition_Album_Cover.jpg/250px-Exclusive_-_The_Forever_Edition_Album_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bc/Exclusive_-_The_Forever_Edition_Album_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bc/Exclusive_-_The_Forever_Edition_Album_Cover.jpg/250px-Ex